 "new_string": "### Additional confirmed instance: paired rays diverge from adjacent color pairs\nA 23x21 test with uniform background 4 had adjacent diagonal pairs: color 9 at `(15,11),(16,10)` and color 2 at `(15,12),(16,13)`, with unrelated singleton colors 5 at `(14,11)` and 8 at `(14,12)`. Correct output extended the 9 pair down-left through `(17,9)` to `(22,4)`, and the 2 pair down-right through `(17,14)` to `(22,19)`. The two rays diverge outward from the compact motif; preserve the original cells and leave the singleton 5 and 8 unchanged. This confirms multiple distinct diagonal color-pairs in one motif can each generate a ray in their outward directions, extending to their respective grid edges.\n\nThis task-specific note is based on correct recurring instances plus demonstrations; treat it as a strong prior, re-derive directions and eligible motifs from every fresh grid, and validate all dimensions and changed coordinates."
